  "legacyCommit": "4deabc5a",
  "purpose": "Doc 06 §1's D58/D68 scan, recorded so the canonical field registry can freeze. Every legacy workflow input schema, roster header rule, OCR form field, and Edit-Data editable field is listed with exactly one disposition: a canonical field id, or workflow-local WITH a reason. `intake-canonical-field-registry.test.ts` fails in BOTH directions — a registry field with no source here is unevidenced vocabulary, and a source field with no disposition is a field that was silently omitted.",
  "localReasons": {
    "execution-option": "an operator-chosen execution knob, not business data — it selects how a run behaves and never becomes a cell in a spreadsheet",
    "file-or-artifact-ref": "a file, page, or artifact reference; doc 06 §1 keeps file refs, selectors, options, and discriminants out of the mappable vocabulary and doc 04 §4.1 routes them through the content-addressed artifact boundary instead",
    "correlation-id": "a run/session/group correlation id assigned by the kernel or the dashboard, never by the operator and never by a source file",
    "run-produced": "produced by the run itself (a match verdict, a warning, an operator selection, a captured screenshot); it is contract output, not intake input, and its shape is owned by the producing contract",
    "computed-from-canonical": "derived arithmetically from canonical fields the same input already carries; mapping it separately would let a stale copy disagree with its own inputs",
    "composite-of-canonical": "an object whose leaves are already canonical fields; the mapping binds the leaves, so binding the wrapper too would let one binding overwrite the other",
    "constant": "a fixed system constant supplied by the descriptor, not by the source file",
    "report-parameter": "a report window the operator types once per run; it bounds a query rather than describing a person",
    "needs-reviewed-type": "the legacy shape conflates values that need a reviewed domain type before any column may be bound to them; the consuming migration owns that decision",
    "crm-verification-flag": "a cross-system verification verdict the run reads from CRM; an operator edit records a correction to what was read, not an intake binding"
  },
